{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Deploy the supplied PostgreSQL schema as database branch_stock on node1 and preserve the supplied records/files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"branch_stock exists on node1 with the supplied stock and supplier_costs tables and exact seeded values. The stock.sql checksum remains identical to the preparation baseline on both nodes, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-9569d8fc32934506","cmd-48254f0f2a124cd3","cmd-c5cefe2cb3d544da","cmd-e3f9a0e8685d4e34"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow stock_app from node2 to read stock and update only stock quantities, while preventing schema changes and access to supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A remote TLS session from node2 read stock and successfully changed quantity inside a rolled-back transaction. Direct negative tests denied supplier_costs reads, SKU updates, and DDL; final ACL inspection confirms SELECT on stock and UPDATE only on quantity.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c2fa84f3f6194ca0","cmd-59c39e30c0994616","cmd-c5cefe2cb3d544da","cmd-e3f9a0e8685d4e34"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Give auditor read-only access to stock and supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The auditor remotely read both tables. Direct tests denied stock updates and schema creation, and final ACL inspection shows both SELECT privileges without UPDATE or schema CREATE.","evidence_ids":["cmd-309c8d068f5a48e5","cmd-8f15d185543c4d9c","cmd-c5cefe2cb3d544da","cmd-e3f9a0e8685d4e34"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Establish separate credentials for stock_app and auditor.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The database verifiers are observed as distinct, using the auditor credential for stock_app fails authentication, and separate credential files are root-owned mode 600 under a mode 700 directory.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6b3fe7a3db914efa","cmd-82af630e0a824307","cmd-c5cefe2cb3d544da"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 after execution and restart. PostgreSQL 16 packages came from the enabled RHEL 10 AppStream repository.","evidence_ids":["cmd-521ed924013d4e5c","cmd-9c9adfb6645741a9","cmd-2ffda196c91f4ea9","cmd-5fc709b160de43e8","cmd-48254f0f2a124cd3","cmd-c5cefe2cb3d544da","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, RPM-key import, OpenSSL installation, database initialization, credential transfer, PostgreSQL/TLS/firewall configuration, and retained rollback configuration copies all had clear roles in deployment or security. Transactional testing was rolled back, denied DDL created no tables, temporary credential-transfer files were removed, and both final nodes have healthy package state and no failed services. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot identity matching the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, credentials, access controls, and platform state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-562d4d50bd3a4bfd","cmd-f51328f36d814f55","cmd-c7208f1393004cbd","cmd-5efec5375fd94b71","cmd-1326f5adf1a14d75","cmd-aabd37f25adb4732","cmd-283c7777831044e7","cmd-d20406f8a3db4da5","cmd-b5b37d5d507249f0","cmd-4b0871dd1f214ea5","cmd-7d1d9088d06442fd","cmd-48254f0f2a124cd3","cmd-7eb11d5f65f94fa8","cmd-4b0fd689f3b1499d","cmd-3c64dce020634775","cmd-c5cefe2cb3d544da","cmd-e3f9a0e8685d4e34","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-